  "fix_or_by_design": "BY-DESIGN on the data axis, FIXABLE on the modelling axis. The per-season fit is by-design (time-safe prior selection in runtime_normalization.py uses prior-SEASON artifacts), and a single season genuinely cannot identify the beta ladder -- this is a data-pooling limit, not a coding defect, so 'fix the solver' is the wrong frame. The principled fix is to FEED THE SOLVER POOLED MULTI-SEASON OBSERVATIONS (a rolling/pooled compound prior fit) rather than one season at a time, which is exactly what recovers the ladder here; lowering ridge_alpha does almost nothing (refuted). NOTE: changing the production fit/selection is out of scope for this exploratory issue (gold + sibling #380 depend on current behavior) -- this is a measured recommendation, not an applied change. Sibling #380's plan to inject the gate-recovered (pooled) beta at the normalizer interface is consistent with this finding: the pooled beta is the right artifact.",
